WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.682
Delivery type is a beginner tradeoff, not a forever identity.

00:00:03.682 --> 00:00:06.996
This lesson is about digital vs service vs hybrid.

00:00:06.996 --> 00:00:08.100
Tradeoffs for beginners.

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:10.678
Do not treat this as theory only.

00:00:10.678 --> 00:00:14.360
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:19.883
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

00:00:19.883 --> 00:00:23.933
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

00:00:23.933 --> 00:00:29.088
Stay practical: choose a delivery type for v1 before you optimize branding or tools.

00:00:29.408 --> 00:00:30.541
Digital scales later.

00:00:30.541 --> 00:00:31.674
Service teaches fast.

00:00:31.674 --> 00:00:34.317
Hybrid mixes a product with human help.

00:00:34.317 --> 00:00:37.716
Remember the objective: choose a delivery type for v1.

00:00:37.716 --> 00:00:41.870
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:46.402
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:00:46.402 --> 00:00:50.556
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:00:50.556 --> 00:00:55.088
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:00:55.408 --> 00:01:00.292
Choose a delivery type for version one based on speed to first paid customer.

